# Shell scripts that run INSIDE the Linux container must keep LF endings.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone gets CRLF and the container dies at startup with
# "exec ./docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory" — the file is there,
# but its shebang reads as "#!/bin/sh\r" and no such interpreter exists. The
# message names the script, so the obvious reading is that it is missing.
# Measured on 2026-08-13 while reproducing a deployment on Windows.
#
# Anyone cloning on Linux never sees this, which is why it went unnoticed.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
